{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/php/antlr/linked_harness.cljc | head -240\nrg -n 'eval' docs/design/yang.php.md | head -30\ncat collab/yang-php/1794624122-engineer-eval-bridge-r13.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md | head -100\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.php.antlr.linked-harness\n  \"The linked profile's composition for the PHP tests (P6, docs/design/\n   yang.php.md section 11): the namespace that requires this is the\n   publisher of `php`, so it publishes the module once per process into one\n   in-memory content store, publishes a fixture's non-entry units beside it\n   bottom-up, and serves them to the entry unit's run over a\n   `yin.vm.linker.interpreter` composition under `:trusted` derivation.\n\n   A linked run builds the entry unit's task on one of the three vector VMs\n   with a link pair, then runs the VM and serves the pair alternately until\n   the VM stops blocking, as the REPL's drive does. The AST walker is not a\n   backend here: its link of `php` is refused until L-b.\"\n  (:require\n    [dao.jing.mem :as mem]\n    [yang.core.call :as call]\n    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as lower]\n    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as portable]\n    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n    [yang.php.antlr.publication :as publication]\n    [yang.php.antlr.safepoint :as safepoint]\n    [yang.php.antlr.siteset :as siteset]\n    [yang.safepoint :as sp]\n    [yin.vm :as vm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n    [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n    [yin.vm.linker.interpreter :as link]\n    [yin.vm.linker.publish :as publish]\n    [yin.vm.linker.sign :as sign]\n    [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.derive :as derive]\n    [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as sr-linearize]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(defn registry\n  \"The host registry a linked PHP composition registers: the `require`\n   handlers, then `cell`, `data` and `integer` under the portable limits.\"\n  []\n  (portable/linked-registry))\n\n\n(defn make-published\n  \"Create a store with the linked runtime and its hook module.\"\n  []\n  (let [store (mem/create-content-mem)\n        call-result (publish/publish-module! store (call/module-spec (registry)))\n        result (publish/publish-module! store (prelude/module-spec (registry)\n                                                                   (:address call-result)))\n        hook (publish/publish-module! store (safepoint/module-spec (registry) (:address result)))]\n    {:store store,\n     :hook-address (:address hook),\n     :result result,\n     :address (:address result),\n     :call-address (:address call-result)}))\n\n\n(def published\n  \"`yang.call` and `php` published once into their own content store.\"\n  (delay (make-published)))\n\n\n(defn publish-units!\n  \"`units` (`[{:name path :packet p :strict-types b}]`) published into\n   `php`'s own content store, where its pinned requirement already lives:\n   `publication/publish-units!`'s answer.\"\n  [units]\n  (publication/publish-units! (:store @published) (registry) (:address @published) units))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"The linked store and signed site publications for this fixture.\"\n  ([name-env] (source name-env nil))\n  ([name-env result]\n   (let [publisher (sign/generate)\n         entries (siteset/signed-entries publisher (:sites result)\n                                         (:addresses result) (:bundles result))\n         datoms (siteset/entry-datoms entries)\n         stage (siteset/stage (registry)\n                              {:hooks true, :hooks-profile safepoint/ticks-profile,\n                               :php-sp (:hook-address @published)} {})]\n     (link/composition\n       {:content-store (:store @published),\n        :name-env (merge {'php (:address @published),\n                          'php.sp (:hook-address @published),\n                          'yang.call (:call-address @published)} name-env),\n        :derivation :trusted,\n        :stage (fn [ctx name address]\n                 (stage (assoc ctx :datoms datoms :principals [(:public publisher)])\n                        name address))}))))\n\n\n(def backends\n  \"Each vector backend's root task over a program AST and composition.\"\n  {:semantic (fn [ast opts]\n               (semantic/load-ast (semantic/create-vm opts)\n                                  (vm/ast->datoms ast)\n                                  vm/ast-contract)),\n   :stack (fn [ast opts]\n            (dvm/create-vm (:image (derive/stack-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast))))\n                           (assoc opts :contract vm/stack-contract))),\n   :register (fn [ast opts]\n               (rvm/create-vm (derive/register-image (:vector (sr-linearize/project ast)))\n                              (assoc opts :contract vm/register-contract)))})\n\n\n(defn composition\n  \"A task's composition over `modules` and the link `pair`.\"\n  [modules pair]\n  {:make-stream tu/make-stream,\n   :capability-secret tu/secret,\n   :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin))),\n   :primitives vm/primitives,\n   :modules modules,\n   :link-request (:requests pair),\n   :link-response (:responses pair)})\n\n\n(defn drive\n  \"Run `task` and serve `pair` from `src` alternately until the task stops\n   blocking, at most 80 rounds. Returns `[task pair]`.\"\n  [task pair src]\n  (loop [task (vm/run task)\n         pair pair\n         i 0]\n    (if (and (vm/blocked? task) (< i 80))\n      (let [pair (:pair (link/serve {:pair pair, :source src}))]\n        (recur (vm/run task) pair (inc i)))\n      [task pair])))\n\n\n(defn run-linked\n  \"The finished task of the linked program `ast` on `backend`, served from\n   `src`. A refused link surfaces as the program's own diagnostics.\"\n  [backend ast src]\n  (let [pair (link/make-pair)\n        task ((get backends backend) ast (composition (registry) pair))]\n    (first (drive task pair src))))\n\n\n(defn name-env\n  \"The name environment naming every published module of `result`\n   (`publish-units!`'s answer): module symbol to address.\"\n  [result]\n  (merge (into {} (map (fn [[path address]] [(lower/path-module-symbol path) address]))\n               (:addresses result))\n         (:bundles result)))\n\n\n(defn run-fixture\n  \"`{backend value}` for the multi-unit fixture `units` (`{path packet}`,\n   the entry unit `main`, default `lower/entry-path`) on the three vector\n   VMs: the non-entry units are published bottom-up, the entry unit\n   lowered `:linked` and run. `value` is `run-main`'s map.\"\n  ([units] (run-fixture units lower/entry-path {}))\n  ([units main opts]\n   (let [entry (get units main)\n         others (cond-> (mapv (fn [[path packet]] {:name path, :packet packet})\n                              (dissoc units main))\n                  (:class-map opts) (conj (assoc (:class-map opts) :name lower/classmap-name)))\n         result (publish-units! others)]\n     (when-not (= :ok (:status result))\n       (throw (ex-info \"fixture units failed to publish\" {:result result})))\n     (let [{:keys [ast warnings]}\n           (lower/lower-program entry\n                                (cond-> (merge {:prelude :linked,\n                                                :path main,\n                                                :paths (when (:computed? opts) (keys (:addresses result)))}\n                                               (dissoc opts :computed? :src :request))\n                                  (:class-map opts) (assoc :class-map true)\n                                  (some? (:request opts)) (assoc :request-node\n                                                                 (portable/request-node (:request opts)))))\n           src (or (:src opts) (source (name-env result) result))\n           sites (:set (siteset/site-set-of ast))\n           tree (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode ast)\n           ast (u/seq-nodes [(core-module/require-node 'yang.call)\n                             (core-module/require-node 'php)\n                             (core-module/require-node 'php.sp)\n                             (vm/semantic-bytecode->ast\n                               (:tree (sp/insert tree (into {} sites) safepoint/ticks-profile)))])]\n       {:warnings warnings,\n        :values (into {}\n                      (map (fn [k] [k (vm/value (run-linked k ast src))]))\n                      (keys backends))}))))\n93:four evaluators and linked on three until L-b), and the ADR 0004 dependency.\n159:  keys at that argument's place in left-to-right order; (2) evaluates every\n191:  arbitrary expression evaluated **when execution first reaches the\n195:  `eval`, or one-argument `parse_str` keeps its locals in a heap symbol-table\n290:  created at class evaluation, with `cases()`, `from`, `tryFrom` and interface\n358:### 3.12 eval\n360:`eval` is a new compilation request (`yang.antlr.md` 8.6) sharing the caller's\n362:with `:yang.php/unsupported :eval` until its slice (P9).\n364:The eval bridge design preserves the exact PHP byte-string source and admits\n369:classified unsupported eval/source-encoding refusal outside guest Throwable\n373:The recorded eval class collision is an uncatchable guest compile fatal, not\n378:ordering require their pinned oracle fixtures. Successful eval declarations\n383:configured compiler service. A composition without one retains the eval refusal.\n384:These are bridge requirements, not a claim that eval execution has landed.\n686:| 13 | by-value parameter                 | row 33 or 34 at evaluation, moved  |\n690:| 14 | by-reference parameter             | row 35 at evaluation               |\n768:|    |                                    | A method call evaluates its        |\n775:|    |                                    | evaluated); (2) refuse abstract    |\n778:|    |                                    | evaluated); (3) create the object  |\n793:|    |                                    | still evaluated and acquired in    |\n799:| 56 | spread argument `f(...$xs)`        | the iterable is evaluated and each |\n821:|    |                                    | just-evaluated value is released   |\n852:|    | (`DO_FCALL` with                   | parameter's default, evaluated in  |\n1449:`declare(encoding)`; `__halt_compiler`; `eval` until its slice; `$$` and\n1636:|            | `eval` pending its run-time    | {:construct}`                  |\n2005:acceptance line runs bundled on four evaluators and linked on three until L-b,\n2140:|       | II, arrays II, JSON, math II),   | parity; `eval` shares the         |\n2142:|       | the dynamic scope, `eval` as a   | corners C5, C6 (prefer-ref), C11, |\n2598:  evaluation (pending calls), uninitialized and readonly typed references,\n2607:  own evaluation, and initialization clearing the clone flag.\nCreated-GMT: 2026-11-14 02:42 UTC\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending\nRole: Engineer\n\n# Eval redeclaration: partial implementation, not ready to land\n\nThe eval entry now binds early functions and classes in source order in the\ncaller, without lowering-time rejection of duplicate top-level functions.\nFunction collisions enter the guest-fatal path, with errno 64 for early\nfunction binding and errno 1 for reached runtime declarations. Class collision\nalso enters that path, with errno 64. Class hoists use per-invocation cells so\nreusing an entry cannot mistake an existing class for its own successful hoist.\nThe existing non-eval compile-time duplicate check remains in place.\n\nRed-first: the new duplicate-function emitter test failed with\n`Cannot redeclare F()` during lowering, then passed after the change. The\nemitter namespace's original tests and that test passed (6 tests, 19\nassertions). Focused direct-entry tests passed on all four VMs for retained\nfunction registration prefix and reusing an entry with a class. A focused\nwalker lifecycle test checked shutdown visibility, status 255, skipped\ncatch/finally, suppressed destructor output and compile-fatal errno. The\nexisting published-eval site-admission test passed. Kondo and cljstyle passed\non the final edited files.\n\nThis is **not** the requested 11-fixture matrix. The two direct-entry cases\ndo not run through service publication and linker admission. The remainder of\nthe matrix, diagnostic locations, the full existing eval suites and portable\nlane have not been verified. The actual PHP eval expression remains explicitly\nunsupported; the requested caller-task `php/eval-run` expression integration\nis described as the next slice, so neither expression path can currently be\nexercised end to end. Do not push or treat this as a green implementation.\nNo PHP oracle was available locally. A mistaken invocation of the test runner\nattempted test discovery and failed on missing generated Python ANTLR classes;\nfocused tests were subsequently run via a test-path alias.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
