{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'php/eval-run|code/entry' collab/yang-php docs -g '*.md' | head -75\"","aggregated_output":"collab/yang-php/1794612969000-engineer-eval-bridge-r11c.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:3:The referenced r11 brief (`1794611409000-engineer-eval-bridge-r11.prompt.md`) is absent from this checkout, so its exact scope and timeout requirements could not be verified. The WIP commit already connects the stream coordinator to eval-unit publication and optional safepoint derivation, and supplies service fixtures and a harness service constructor. The focused service fixture verifies publication, derivation, linker admission and retrieval of an installed entry closure. It does not demonstrate executing eval in a caller task; `php/eval-run`, expression lowering and a harness driver for guest requests remain outstanding. This is not a completed end-to-end eval bridge.\ncollab/yang-php/1794605712000-architect-bytedomain-ruling.findings.md:149:Unchanged architectural properties confirmed: no parser calls from portable execution; no caller state in compile requests; no second runtime or budget; ordinary code/entry/link admission; same-task cell ownership; exact source provenance; no shared mutable compiler state. This ruling authorizes design direction, not implementation sign-off.\ncollab/yang-php/1794607599000-engineer-eval-bridge-r7.prompt.md:12:compile request/response transport and artifact publication; installed manifest-pinned code/entry;\ncollab/yang-php/1794607599000-engineer-eval-bridge-r7.prompt.md:13:php/eval-run in caller task; both expression paths; atomic redeclaration through guest fatal;\ncollab/yang-php/1794607460000-engineer-eval-bridge-r6.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:9:Remaining: implement and test the eval-unit emitter and runtime import/hook bindings; compile request/response transport and artifact publication; installed manifest-pinned `code/entry`; `php/eval-run` in caller task; both expression paths; atomic redeclaration checks through guest fatal; caller scope and budget integration; the requested real-service fixtures and all named gates. The current e2e harness has no configured eval compiler service, so simply changing the refusal would not constitute a working bridge. This round does not meet the definition of done.\ncollab/yang-php/1794624313000-engineer-eval-bridge-r13r3.prompt.md:22:   scope-cleanup/retention) stay green; php/eval-run in the caller task if budget allows,\ncollab/yang-php/1794606615000-engineer-eval-bridge-r4.prompt.md:20:4. php/eval-run stream-effect + correlated outcome; the two refusal paths replaced.\ncollab/yang-php/1794606615000-engineer-eval-bridge-r4.prompt.md:21:5. code/entry retrieval effect.\ncollab/yang-php/1794614072000-engineer-eval-bridge-r12.prompt.md:6:# Task: eval-bridge r12 — php/eval-run in the caller task + both expression paths + atomic redeclaration\ncollab/yang-php/1794614072000-engineer-eval-bridge-r12.prompt.md:11:1. php/eval-run in the caller task: the caller's runtime supplies the stream-effect request; the installed entry executes IN THE CALLER TASK against caller cells/scope/budget; the outcome correlates back through the stream; fall-through maps to :php/null.\ncollab/yang-php/1794611409000-engineer-eval-bridge-r11.prompt.md:20:   linker admission (the site-set stage from P7-b) -> installed entry available via code/entry.\ncollab/yang-php/1794611409000-engineer-eval-bridge-r11.prompt.md:22:   retrievable via code/entry; malformed/ill-formed payload -> classified refusal through the\ncollab/yang-php/1794611409000-engineer-eval-bridge-r11.prompt.md:29:php/eval-run + expression paths + redeclaration: NOT this slice (r12).\ncollab/yang-php/1794608699000-engineer-eval-bridge-r8.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:11:The bridge remains incomplete: request/response transport and service-backed admission/publication, caller-task `php/eval-run` including scope/budget, both expression routes, atomic guest compile fatal, real-service fixtures and the full gate set remain outstanding. The standalone publisher is not an admission decision. No end-to-end eval support is claimed. Node/Dart and lint validation remain outstanding.\ncollab/yang-php/1794611295000-engineer-eval-bridge-r10.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:7:The requested bridge is not complete. The new coordinator entry is not yet wired to a request/response stream; it returns a prepared CST, not a published or admitted entry. The configured compiler service and harness integration, active derivation and linker admission, caller-task `php/eval-run`, both eval expression paths, atomic redeclaration fatal behavior, and service-backed end-to-end fixtures remain outstanding. The named tick, include, generator, lower-portable, publication, and broader gates were not run; no cross-host verification was done. No commit or push was made because the requested green gate was not reached.\ncollab/yang-php/1794600468000-engineer-eval-bridge.prompt.md:14:message: the compilation path (php/eval-run via stream effects; never cst/parse-source or a\ncollab/yang-php/1794600468000-engineer-eval-bridge.prompt.md:19:code/entry retrieval effect (engine effect-handler registry; no new VM opcode), compilation\ncollab/yang-php/1794600468000-engineer-eval-bridge.prompt.md:25:A. Engine: code/entry retrieval effect per design.\ncollab/yang-php/1794600468000-engineer-eval-bridge.prompt.md:28:C. PHP prelude: php/eval-run stream-effect implementation; request shape; correlated outcome.\ncollab/yang-php/1794614848000-engineer-eval-bridge-r13.prompt.md:40:php/eval-run in caller task + expression-path conversion: next slice after this matrix lands.\ncollab/yang-php/1794605992000-engineer-eval-bridge-r2.prompt.md:15:3. The eval-unit emission + php/eval-run + code/entry effect: proceed if budget allows after 1-2; otherwise record precisely for the next slice. (The admission slice is the deliverable; the pipeline may defer.)\ncollab/yang-php/1794608699000-engineer-eval-bridge-r8.prompt.md:15:2. Actual installed accessor execution across backends (the manifest-pinned code/entry effect\ncollab/yang-php/1794608699000-engineer-eval-bridge-r8.prompt.md:17:3. php/eval-run in the caller task (caller cells/scope/budget).\ncollab/yang-php/1794607338000-engineer-eval-bridge-r6.prompt.md:6:# Task: eval-bridge part 6 — eval-unit emission + collision fatal + php/eval-run\ncollab/yang-php/1794607338000-engineer-eval-bridge-r6.prompt.md:13:2. php/eval-run: stream-effect compilation request (source bytes, request identity, revisions, eval goal, provenance, options; NO caller cells/continuation/host handles) -> correlated outcome; the eval-unit installed entry called in the caller task against caller cells/budget.\ncollab/yang-php/1794607338000-engineer-eval-bridge-r6.prompt.md:14:3. code/entry retrieval effect: declared export from an installed manifest-pinned module (engine effect-handler registry; no new VM opcode); try-require returns the name, not exports.\ncollab/yang-php/1794624540000-engineer-eval-bridge-r14.prompt.md:10:REFUSE eval (lower.cljc); php/eval-run + code/entry unimplemented. Six sessions have delivered\ncollab/yang-php/1794624540000-engineer-eval-bridge-r14.prompt.md:18:2. php/eval-run: minimal stream-effect implementation per design §4 (request shape per the\ncollab/yang-php/1794624540000-engineer-eval-bridge-r14.prompt.md:20:3. code/entry: the manifest-pinned retrieval effect (part 7's installed-export effect already\ncollab/yang-php/1794624456000-engineer-eval-bridge-r13r3.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:17:The two expression lowering paths still refuse eval; there is no `php/eval-run`.\ncollab/yang-php/1794606837-engineer-eval-bridge-r4.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:9:The compiler coordinator, PHP-mode eval source goal, source-aware validation and byte/revision identity integration, eval-unit emission, collision handling, `php/eval-run`, and `code/entry` remain unimplemented. Both lowering refusal paths remain. The current generic PHP parser starts at `htmlDocument`; there is no existing eval compiler coordinator in the source tree. The required end-to-end fixtures and gates remain outstanding. This checkpoint does not make eval executable.\ncollab/yang-php/1794608331000-engineer-eval-bridge-r7.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:11:Remaining: compile request/response transport and service-backed admission/publication, actual installed accessor execution across backends, `php/eval-run` in the caller task, both expression paths, atomic redeclaration via guest fatal, caller scope and budget integration, generator dictionary cleanup, real-service fixtures and all named gates. Source/site records need integration into the authenticated derivation and admission path; the standalone publisher is not an admission decision. Verify the eval site profile in that integration: the reused site publication currently labels its profile as linked PHP module, while eval hooks are local aliases. The e2e harness still has no configured eval compiler service. No end-to-end eval support or P9 completion is claimed.\ncollab/yang-php/1794611156000-engineer-eval-bridge-r10.prompt.md:6:# Task: eval-bridge part 10 — the CORE: compile-request transport + service-backed admission/publication + php/eval-run + both expression paths + atomic redeclaration\ncollab/yang-php/1794611156000-engineer-eval-bridge-r10.prompt.md:11:1. Compile request/response transport: the request (source bytes, request identity, revisions, eval goal, provenance, options; NO caller cells/values/continuation/host handles) -> parser worker (eval source goal, PHP-mode lexer via the committed coordinator path) -> CST validation+scope analysis -> eval-unit emission -> canonical envelope -> active safepoint derivation -> publication + linker admission (ordinary machinery) -> installed entry available via code/entry.\ncollab/yang-php/1794611156000-engineer-eval-bridge-r10.prompt.md:13:3. php/eval-run in the caller task: stream-effect request -> correlated outcome -> installed entry called in the caller task against caller cells/scope/budget; fall-through :php/null; caller runtime via %runtime inventory (part 7's caller runtime inventory).\ncollab/yang-php/1794624122-engineer-eval-bridge-r13.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:30:unsupported; the requested caller-task `php/eval-run` expression integration\ncollab/yang-php/1794606466000-engineer-eval-bridge-r3.prompt.md:6:# Task: eval-bridge part 3 — wire admission into the compiler coordinator + eval-unit emission + php/eval-run + code/entry\ncollab/yang-php/1794606466000-engineer-eval-bridge-r3.prompt.md:15:3. php/eval-run: stream-effect request -> correlated outcome; called in the caller's task with caller scope/context/budget; the two refusal paths (prefix + plain-call) replaced.\ncollab/yang-php/1794606466000-engineer-eval-bridge-r3.prompt.md:16:4. code/entry retrieval effect (existing effect-handler registry; no new VM opcode).\ncollab/yang-php/1794605992000-engineer-eval-bridge-r2.gpt-6.1-terra.findings.md:30:Implement the actual stream-driven compiler coordinator and eval source goal in PHP mode with the default lexer mode underneath, without synthetic tags. Wire `admit-request` before parse and confirm envelope names against the coordinator protocol; pass the decoded Unicode view to both parser and source-aware validation, retain original bytes and profile revision in identity/lookup. Add complete byte-span, line-table, transport-chunk and cross-host tests, oracle-pending fixtures and actual PHP oracle runs. Then implement eval-unit emission, `php/eval-run`, code/entry, caller scope/budget and the ruled declaration/fatal behavior. Complete the timed-out lowering and all remaining focused gates before calling the admission slice complete.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
